IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Qualifying for Benefits": ss 7, 7.1 and 8. Layer 1 of piece ei1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Conventions as in ei1-interpretation.l4: a rate is a fraction (6.5% is 0.065), the regional rate that applies to a
-- person is an input (Regulations reg 17, piece er1), the hours of insurable employment are an input (s 6(3)), a
-- week is identified by the DATE of its Sunday, and a limit in weeks goes through `weeks as days` in the core.

§ `Section 7 - qualifying`

-- src:159 | 7 (1) Unemployment benefits are payable as provided in this Part to an insured person who qualifies to receive them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(1) (src:159)
GIVEN `the person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person qualifies to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable as provided in Part I to the insured person` IF
        `the person is an insured person`
    AND `the insured person qualifies to receive them`

-- src:162 | (a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and
-- "Interruption of earnings" is defined by the Regulations (reg 14 and reg 14.01, piece er1); the result is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(2)(a) (src:162)
GIVEN -- out of range: reg 14 and reg 14.01 (piece er1)
      `an interruption of earnings has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(2)(a) the insured person has had an interruption of earnings from employment` IF
    `an interruption of earnings has occurred`

-- src:165 | Regional Rate of Unemployment | Required Number of Hours of Insurable Employment in Qualifying Period
-- src:166 | 6% and under | 700
-- src:167 | more than 6% but not more than 7% | 665
-- src:168 | more than 7% but not more than 8% | 630
-- src:169 | more than 8% but not more than 9% | 595
-- src:170 | more than 9% but not more than 10% | 560
-- src:171 | more than 10% but not more than 11% | 525
-- src:172 | more than 11% but not more than 12% | 490
-- src:173 | more than 12% but not more than 13% | 455
-- src:174 | more than 13% | 420
-- The table is read in nine bands; the core's twelve-band `Rate band` has bands 9 to 12 together as "more than 13%".
-- The regional rate that applies to the person is decided by reg 17 and Schedule I of the Regulations (pieces er1, er6).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(2)(b) table (src:165-174)
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7(2)(b) the number of hours of insurable employment required in relation to the regional rate of unemployment` IS
    CONSIDER `the band of the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person`
    WHEN `6% and under`                          THEN 700
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`     THEN 665
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`     THEN 630
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`     THEN 595
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`    THEN 560
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%`   THEN 525
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%`   THEN 490
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%`   THEN 455
    OTHERWISE 420

-- src:163 | (b) has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours of insurable employment set out in the following table in relation to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(2)(b) (src:163)
GIVEN `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours of insurable employment required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(2)(b) the insured person has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours required` IF
    `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST `the number of hours of insurable employment required`

-- src:161 | (2) An insured person qualifies if the person
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(2) (src:161)
GIVEN `the insured person has had an interruption of earnings from employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(2) an insured person qualifies` IF
        `the insured person has had an interruption of earnings from employment`
    AND `the insured person has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours required`

-- s 7(3) to (5): [Repealed, 2016, c. 7, s. 209] (src line 175). Nothing to encode.

-- src:177 | (6) An insured person is not qualified to receive benefits if it is jointly determined that the insured person must first exhaust or end benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942.
-- The agreement is Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance,
-- signed on March 6 and 12, 1942. Whether it is "jointly determined" is a decision of the two states: an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(6) (src:177)
GIVEN `it is jointly determined that the insured person must first exhaust or end benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction as provided by Article VI of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(6) the insured person is not qualified to receive benefits because of the Canada-U.S. agreement` IF
    `it is jointly determined that the insured person must first exhaust or end benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction as provided by Article VI of the Agreement`

§ `Section 7.1 - increase in required hours`

-- A violation, as the person in the seat would state it: its class, the day it was accumulated (the day the notice of
-- violation was issued, s 7.1(4); for a violation accumulated under s 152.07, the day the notice was given, s 7.1(2.1)),
-- and the number of earlier initial claims in which it was taken into account and the individual qualified (s 7.1(3)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(2.1), s 7.1(3), s 7.1(4), s 7.1(5) (src:194) (src:196) (src:198-201) (src:203-207)
DECLARE `ei1 Violation` HAS
    `ei1 the class of the violation`                                           IS A `Violation class`
    `ei1 the day on which the violation was accumulated`                       IS A DATE
    `ei1 the earlier initial claims in which it was taken into account and the individual qualified` IS A NUMBER

-- src:183 | 6% and under/6 % et moins | 875 | 1050 | 1225 | 1400
-- src:184 | more than 6% but not more than 7%/plus de 6 % mais au plus 7 % | 831 | 998 | 1164 | 1330
-- src:185 | more than 7% but not more than 8%/plus de 7 % mais au plus 8 % | 788 | 945 | 1103 | 1260
-- src:186 | more than 8% but not more than 9%/plus de 8 % mais au plus 9 % | 744 | 893 | 1041 | 1190
-- src:187 | more than 9% but not more than 10%/plus de 9 % mais au plus 10 % | 700 | 840 | 980 | 1120
-- src:188 | more than 10% but not more than 11%/plus de 10 % mais au plus 11 % | 656 | 788 | 919 | 1050
-- src:189 | more than 11% but not more than 12%/plus de 11 % mais au plus 12 % | 613 | 735 | 858 | 980
-- src:190 | more than 12% but not more than 13%/plus de 12 % mais au plus 13 % | 569 | 683 | 796 | 910
-- src:191 | more than 13%/plus de 13 % | 525 | 630 | 735 | 840
-- One row of the table: the hours required for each class of violation, at one band of the regional rate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1) table (src:183-191)
DECLARE `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` HAS
    `ei1 hours for a minor violation`       IS A NUMBER
    `ei1 hours for a serious violation`     IS A NUMBER
    `ei1 hours for a very serious violation` IS A NUMBER
    `ei1 hours for a subsequent violation`  IS A NUMBER

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1) table (src:183-191)
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `ei1 Hours required by class of violation`
DECIDE `s 7.1(1) the row of the table for the regional rate of unemployment` IS
    CONSIDER `the band of the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person`
    --                                                                                    minor, serious, very serious, subsequent
    WHEN `6% and under`                          THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 875, 1050, 1225, 1400
    WHEN `more than 6% but not more than 7%`     THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 831,  998, 1164, 1330
    WHEN `more than 7% but not more than 8%`     THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 788,  945, 1103, 1260
    WHEN `more than 8% but not more than 9%`     THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 744,  893, 1041, 1190
    WHEN `more than 9% but not more than 10%`    THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 700,  840,  980, 1120
    WHEN `more than 10% but not more than 11%`   THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 656,  788,  919, 1050
    WHEN `more than 11% but not more than 12%`   THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 613,  735,  858,  980
    WHEN `more than 12% but not more than 13%`   THEN `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 569,  683,  796,  910
    OTHERWISE                                         `ei1 Hours required by class of violation` OF 525,  630,  735,  840

-- src:179 | 7.1 (1) The number of hours that an insured person requires under section 7 to qualify for benefits is increased to the number set out in the following table in relation to the applicable regional rate of unemployment if the insured person accumulates one or more violations in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1) (src:179)
GIVEN class IS A `Violation class`
      row IS A `ei1 Hours required by class of violation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(1) the number of hours set out in the table for the class of the violation` IS
    CONSIDER class
    WHEN `a minor violation`        THEN row's `ei1 hours for a minor violation`
    WHEN `a serious violation`      THEN row's `ei1 hours for a serious violation`
    WHEN `a very serious violation` THEN row's `ei1 hours for a very serious violation`
    WHEN `a subsequent violation`   THEN row's `ei1 hours for a subsequent violation`

-- src:179 | 7.1 (1) The number of hours that an insured person requires under section 7 to qualify for benefits is increased to the number set out in the following table in relation to the applicable regional rate of unemployment if the insured person accumulates one or more violations in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits.
-- "In the 260 weeks before making their initial claim": the 260 weeks (1,820 days) that end on the day before the
-- initial claim is made. The day of the claim itself is not before it. Assumed, not ruled (fork F-window in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1) (src:179)
GIVEN `the day on which the violation was accumulated` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the insured person makes the initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7.1(1) the violation was accumulated in the 260 weeks before the initial claim` IF
        `the day on which the violation was accumulated` AT LEAST (`the day on which the insured person makes the initial claim for benefits` MINUS `weeks as days` 260)
    AND `the day on which the violation was accumulated` BELOW `the day on which the insured person makes the initial claim for benefits`

-- src:194 | (2.1) A violation accumulated by an individual under section 152.07 is deemed to be a violation accumulated by the individual under this section on the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(2.1) (src:194)
GIVEN -- out of range: section 152.07 (piece ei5)
      `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 7.1(2.1) the day on which a violation accumulated under section 152.07 is deemed to be accumulated under section 7.1` IS
    `the day on which the notice of violation was given to the individual`

-- src:196 | (3) A violation may not be taken into account under subsection (1) in more than two initial claims for benefits under this Act by an individual if the individual who accumulated the violation qualified for benefits in each of those two initial claims, taking into account subsection (1), subparagraph 152.07(1)(d)(ii) or regulations made under Part VIII, as the case may be.
-- A violation counts in at most two initial claims in which the individual qualified (counting the claim being
-- decided as the third, a violation already used in two earlier qualifying claims is spent).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(3) (src:196)
GIVEN `the number of earlier initial claims in which the violation was taken into account and the individual qualified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7.1(3) the violation may be taken into account in this initial claim` IF
    `the number of earlier initial claims in which the violation was taken into account and the individual qualified` BELOW 2

-- src:179 | 7.1 (1) The number of hours that an insured person requires under section 7 to qualify for benefits is increased to the number set out in the following table in relation to the applicable regional rate of unemployment if the insured person accumulates one or more violations in the 260 weeks before making their initial claim for benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1), s 7.1(3) (src:179) (src:196)
GIVEN violations IS A LIST OF `ei1 Violation`
      `the day on which the insured person makes the initial claim for benefits` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `Violation class`
DECIDE `s 7.1(1) the classes of the violations that raise the hours required` IS
    map (GIVEN v YIELD v's `ei1 the class of the violation`)
        (filter (GIVEN v YIELD
                      `s 7.1(1) the violation was accumulated in the 260 weeks before the initial claim` (v's `ei1 the day on which the violation was accumulated`) `the day on which the insured person makes the initial claim for benefits`
                  AND `s 7.1(3) the violation may be taken into account in this initial claim` (v's `ei1 the earlier initial claims in which it was taken into account and the individual qualified`))
                violations)

-- With violations of more than one class the Act does not say which column of the table applies. Assumed, not
-- ruled (fork F-several in NOTES.md): the largest figure of the classes in the window. In practice a second violation
-- within 260 weeks of the first is a "subsequent violation" (s 7.1(5)(b)), the last column, which is the largest.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(1) (src:179)
GIVEN classes IS A LIST OF `Violation class`
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(1) the number of hours that an insured person requires` IS
    IF null classes
    THEN `s 7(2)(b) the number of hours of insurable employment required in relation to the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person`
    ELSE maximum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 7.1(1) the number of hours set out in the table for the class of the violation` c (`s 7.1(1) the row of the table for the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person`)) classes)

-- src:161 | (2) An insured person qualifies if the person
-- src:162 | (a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and
-- src:163 | (b) has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours of insurable employment set out in the following table in relation to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the person.
-- src:177 | (6) An insured person is not qualified to receive benefits if it is jointly determined that the insured person must first exhaust or end benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as provided by Article VI of the Agreement Between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7(1), s 7(2), s 7(6), s 7.1(1) (src:161-163) (src:177)
GIVEN `the person is an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person has had an interruption of earnings from employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours of insurable employment required` IS A NUMBER
      `the insured person is not qualified because of the Canada-U.S. agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 and s 7.1 the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` IF
        `the person is an insured person`
    AND `s 7(2) an insured person qualifies` `the insured person has had an interruption of earnings from employment` (`s 7(2)(b) the insured person has had during their qualifying period at least the number of hours required` `the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` `the number of hours of insurable employment required`)
    AND NOT (`the insured person is not qualified because of the Canada-U.S. agreement`)

-- src:198 | (4) An insured person accumulates a violation if in any of the following circumstances the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person:
-- src:199 | (a) one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1, as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1;
-- src:200 | (b) the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections; or
-- src:201 | (c) the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(4) (src:198-201)
GIVEN `the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7.1(4) an insured person accumulates a violation` IF
        `the Commission issues a notice of violation to the person`
    AND (   `one or more penalties are imposed on the person under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1`
         OR `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under section 135 or 136 as a result of acts or omissions mentioned in those sections`
         OR `the person is found guilty of one or more offences under the Criminal Code as a result of acts or omissions relating to the application of the Act`)

-- src:208 | (b) if the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation, it is a subsequent violation, even if the acts or omissions on which it is based occurred before the person accumulated the other violation.
-- "Within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation": the notice is issued after the other violation
-- was accumulated and no more than 1,820 days later. A notice issued on the same day is not "after" it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(5)(b) (src:208)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice of violation is issued` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the person accumulated other violations` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7.1(5)(b) the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` IF
    any (GIVEN other YIELD (other BELOW `the day on which the notice of violation is issued`) AND (`the day on which the notice of violation is issued` AT MOST (other PLUS `weeks as days` 260)))
        `the days on which the person accumulated other violations`

-- src:203 | (5) Except for violations for which a warning was imposed, each violation is classified as a minor, serious, very serious or subsequent violation as follows:
-- src:204 | (a) if the value of the violation is
-- src:205 | (i) less than $1,000, it is a minor violation,
-- src:206 | (ii) $1,000 or more, but less than $5,000, it is a serious violation, or
-- src:207 | (iii) $5,000 or more, it is a very serious violation; and
-- Where both (a) and (b) apply (a notice issued within 260 weeks after another violation, whatever the value), the
-- violation is "a subsequent violation": that is the reading taken (fork F-subsequent in NOTES.md). A violation for
-- which a warning was imposed has no class: s 7.1(5) leaves it out, so the answer is NOTHING, never a class.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(5) (src:203-207)
GIVEN `a warning was imposed for the violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the violation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Violation class`
DECIDE `s 7.1(5) the class of the violation` IS
    BRANCH IF `a warning was imposed for the violation` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` THEN JUST `a subsequent violation`
           IF `the value of the violation` BELOW 1000 THEN JUST `a minor violation`
           IF `the value of the violation` BELOW 5000 THEN JUST `a serious violation`
           OTHERWISE JUST `a very serious violation`

-- src:212 | (b) if the claimant is disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits, or the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under section 7, the amount determined, subject to subsection (7), by multiplying the claimant’s weekly rate of benefit by the average number of weeks of regular benefits, as determined under the regulations.
-- src:213 | Maximum
-- src:214 | (7) The maximum amount to be determined under paragraph (6)(b) is the amount of benefits that could have been paid to the claimant if the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified or had met the qualification requirements under section 7.
-- The weekly rate of benefit is s 14's (below); the average number of weeks of regular benefits is "as determined
-- under the regulations": reg 13(1) (piece er1). The overpayment resulting from the acts or omissions is Part VI's
-- (piece ei4).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(7) (src:214)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of benefit of the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: reg 13(1) (piece er1)
      `the average number of weeks of regular benefits as determined under the regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of benefits that could have been paid to the claimant if the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified or had met the qualification requirements under section 7` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(7) the amount determined under paragraph 7.1(6)(b)` IS
    min (`the weekly rate of benefit of the claimant` TIMES `the average number of weeks of regular benefits as determined under the regulations`)
        `the amount of benefits that could have been paid to the claimant if the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified or had met the qualification requirements under section 7`

-- src:210 | (6) The value of a violation is the total of
-- src:211 | (a) the amount of the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based, and
-- src:212 | (b) if the claimant is disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits, or the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under section 7, the amount determined, subject to subsection (7), by multiplying the claimant’s weekly rate of benefit by the average number of weeks of regular benefits, as determined under the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 7.1(6) (src:210-212)
GIVEN -- out of range: the definition of an overpayment of benefits in Part VI (piece ei4)
      `the amount of the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant is disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount determined under paragraph (6)(b), subject to subsection (7)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 7.1(6) the value of the violation` IS
    `the amount of the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which the violation is based`
    PLUS (IF `the claimant is disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits` OR `the act or omission on which the violation is based relates to qualification requirements under section 7`
          THEN `the amount determined under paragraph (6)(b), subject to subsection (7)`
          ELSE 0)

§ `Section 8 - the qualifying period`

-- src:217 | (a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of a benefit period under subsection 10(1), and
-- Weeks begin on a Sunday and a benefit period begins on one (s 10(1)), so the 52 weeks immediately before it run
-- from the Sunday 364 days earlier to the Saturday before it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(1)(a) (src:217)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`the first day of the benefit period` MINUS `weeks as days` 52), (`the first day of the benefit period` MINUS 1)

-- src:218 | (b) the period that begins on the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period and ends with the end of the week before the beginning of a benefit period under subsection 10(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(1)(b) (src:218)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period`, (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the first day of the benefit period` MINUS 1))

-- src:216 | 8 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (7), the qualifying period of an insured person is the shorter of
-- With no immediately preceding benefit period paragraph (b) has nothing to measure, so the 52-week period of
-- paragraph (a) is the qualifying period (fork F-no-prior in NOTES.md). The "shorter" is judged before any extension;
-- when the two are equally long they are the same period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(1) (src:216)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 8(1) the shorter of the 52-week period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began` IS
    CONSIDER `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period, if there was one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period`
    WHEN JUST prior THEN
        IF `the number of days in` (`s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` prior)
             BELOW `the number of days in` (`s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period`)
        THEN `s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` prior
        ELSE `s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period`

-- src:220 | (2) A qualifying period mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during the qualifying period for which the person proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that throughout the week the person was not employed in insurable employment because the person was
-- src:221 | (a) incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy;
-- src:222 | (b) confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution and was not found guilty of the offence for which the person was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction;
-- src:223 | (c) receiving assistance under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d); or
-- src:224 | (d) receiving payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the person, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding.
-- The person must prove the reason "in such manner as the Commission may direct": the first input is that proof, taken
-- as given. Paragraph (b) needs a person held but not found guilty, so being found guilty is its own input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(2) (src:220-224)
GIVEN `the person proves, in the manner the Commission directs, that throughout the week the person was not employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: reg 40 and reg 41 (piece er3) say which illness, injury or quarantine is prescribed
      `the person was incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was found guilty of the offence for which the person was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving assistance under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 59 (piece ei2)
      `that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the person, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` IF
        `the person proves, in the manner the Commission directs, that throughout the week the person was not employed in insurable employment`
    AND (   `the person was incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy`
         OR (`the person was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` AND NOT (`the person was found guilty of the offence for which the person was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction`))
         OR (`the person was receiving assistance under an employment support measure` AND NOT (`that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)`))
         OR `the person was receiving payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the person, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding`)

-- s 8(3): [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 305] (src line 225). Nothing to encode.

-- src:227 | (4) A qualifying period is further extended by the aggregate of any weeks during an extension for which the person proves, in any manner that the Commission may direct, that the person was not employed in insurable employment because of a reason specified in subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(4) (src:227)
GIVEN `the week falls during an extension of the qualifying period under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(4) the week during an extension further extends the qualifying period` IF
        `the week falls during an extension of the qualifying period under subsection (2)`
    AND `the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period`

-- src:229 | (5) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (4), a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits does not count.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(5) (src:229)
GIVEN `the person was in receipt of benefits during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(5) the week counts for the purposes of subsections 8(2) and 8(4)` IF
    NOT (`the person was in receipt of benefits during the week`)

-- s 8(6): [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 305] (src line 230). Nothing to encode.

-- src:232 | (7) No extension under subsection (2) or (4) may result in a qualifying period of more than 104 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(7) (src:232)
`s 8(7) the longest qualifying period after an extension, in weeks` MEANS 104

-- src:216 | 8 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (7), the qualifying period of an insured person is the shorter of
-- src:217 | (a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of a benefit period under subsection 10(1), and
-- src:218 | (b) the period that begins on the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period and ends with the end of the week before the beginning of a benefit period under subsection 10(1).
-- src:219 | Extension of qualifying period
-- src:220 | (2) A qualifying period mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during the qualifying period for which the person proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that throughout the week the person was not employed in insurable employment because the person was
-- src:221 | (a) incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy;
-- src:222 | (b) confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution and was not found guilty of the offence for which the person was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction;
-- src:223 | (c) receiving assistance under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d); or
-- src:224 | (d) receiving payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the person, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding.
-- src:225 | (3) [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 305]
-- src:226 | Further extension of qualifying period
-- src:227 | (4) A qualifying period is further extended by the aggregate of any weeks during an extension for which the person proves, in any manner that the Commission may direct, that the person was not employed in insurable employment because of a reason specified in subsection (2).
-- src:228 | Period not counted if benefits received
-- src:229 | (5) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (4), a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits does not count.
-- src:230 | (6) [Repealed, 2021, c. 23, s. 305]
-- src:231 | Maximum extension of qualifying period
-- src:232 | (7) No extension under subsection (2) or (4) may result in a qualifying period of more than 104 weeks.
-- The number of weeks that extend the qualifying period are counted once each and after s 8(5): the first count is of
-- weeks during the 52-week period (subsection (2)); the second of weeks during that extension (subsection (4)).
-- An extension applies only to the period in paragraph (1)(a); when the period of paragraph (1)(b) is the shorter,
-- it is the qualifying period as it stands. No extension may make the period longer than 104 weeks (subsection (7)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 8(1), s 8(2), s 8(4), s 8(7) (src:216) (src:220) (src:227) (src:232)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the number of weeks that extend the qualifying period under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks that further extend the qualifying period under subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 8 the qualifying period` IS
    CONSIDER `the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period, if there was one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the 52-week period, extended`
    WHEN JUST prior THEN
        IF `the number of days in` (`s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` prior)
             BELOW `the number of days in` (`s 8(1)(a) the 52-week period immediately before the beginning of the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period`)
        THEN `s 8(1)(b) the period from the first day of an immediately preceding benefit period to the end of the week before the benefit period` `the first day of the benefit period` prior
        ELSE `the 52-week period, extended`
    WHERE
        `the weeks of extension` MEANS
            min (`s 8(7) the longest qualifying period after an extension, in weeks` MINUS 52)
                (`the number of weeks that extend the qualifying period under subsection (2)` PLUS `the number of weeks that further extend the qualifying period under subsection (4)`)
        `the 52-week period, extended` MEANS
            `Period of days` OF (`the first day of the benefit period` MINUS `weeks as days` (52 PLUS `the weeks of extension`)), (`the first day of the benefit period` MINUS 1)
